  "thumbnailUrl": "https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-datasets-images/new-version-temp-images/default-backgrounds-76.png-34185974/dataset-card.png",
  "dateModified": "2026-05-06T18:16:05.167",
  "datePublished": "2026-05-06T17:56:20.6554749",
  "@type": "sc:Dataset",
  "name": "Penmanshiel WT08 Hourly SCADA Time Series Dataset",
  "url": "https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/sensorfaultbench/penmanshiel-wt08-hourly-scada-time-series-dataset/versions/2",
  "citeAs": "@inproceedings{windmann2026benchmarking,\n  title={Benchmarking Sensor-Fault Robustness in Forecasting},\n  author={Windmann, Alexander and Wittenberg, Philipp and Manca, Gianluca and Dix, Marcel and Brandt, Jens U. and Niggemann, Oliver},\n  booktitle={The Fortieth Annual Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems Evaluations and Datasets Track},\n  year={2026},\n  url={https://neurips.cc/virtual/2026/loc/paris/poster/138912}\n}",
  "description": "Derived hourly SCADA time series dataset for turbine WT08 from the Penmanshiel wind farm data collection on Zenodo. Source: https://zenodo.org/records/16807304. The record contains a canonical Parquet benchmark file and CSV mirror for forecasting and sensor-fault robustness evaluation. It uses raw WT08 SCADA, removes leakage-prone channels, selects the longest target-continuous segment, aggregates complete hourly bins from six 10-minute rows, and uses Power (kW) as the downstream forecast target.",
  "dct:conformsTo": "http://mlcommons.org/croissant/RAI/1.0",
  "rai:dataLimitations": "Single-turbine WT08 subset from one wind farm, not a fleet-wide or universal wind-energy dataset. Hourly aggregation and channel pruning remove information from the raw 10-minute SCADA source. The dataset is not recommended for safety certification, operational control, maintenance scheduling, asset valuation, or deployment without site-specific validation.",
  "rai:dataBiases": "The dataset has turbine, site, and retained-segment selection bias. Dropping leakage-prone channels, dropping long-gap channels, and selecting one target-continuous segment may remove variables or periods associated with outages or operating states. Hourly averaging smooths short transients and may underrepresent fast operational changes.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "No personal or human-subject records are included. The data describe turbine SCADA measurements.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": "The dataset is intended for reproducible time series forecasting experiments and sensor-fault robustness benchmarking under the accompanying benchmark protocol. The packaged files do not include sensor-fault labels, corrupted samples, or faulted samples because sensor-fault scenarios are generated by the benchmark code during evaluation. It is not validated for turbine control, maintenance, safety, financial, or operational decision-making.",
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "Positive use is transparent benchmarking on renewable-energy SCADA data. The main risk is mistaking a benchmark slice for operationally certified performance evidence.",
  "rai:hasSyntheticData": false,
  "prov:wasDerivedFrom": "https://zenodo.org/records/16807304",
  "prov:wasGeneratedBy": "Derived from WT08 raw SCADA exports covering 2016 through 2022 by using raw WT08 SCADA only, removing cumulative energy counters, availability or contractual indices, controller expectations, and power-curve helper columns, splitting at Power (kW) gaps longer than one day, selecting the longest target-continuous segment, dropping non-target channels with kept-segment gaps longer than 21 days, forward-filling shorter gaps only inside the retained segment, aggregating complete hourly bins from six 10-minute rows, applying no backward fill, exporting the canonical Parquet file, and packaging it with a CSV mirror and SHA256 checksum manifest."
}
